  "selection_rule": [
    "Fixed before any screening or run.",
    "Slots: Go (gin), Go + DevOps/infrastructure (caddy), Go (grpc-go or go-zero), JavaScript (axios), TypeScript (vuejs/core), large repository (prometheus).",
    "Candidates per slot ranked by sha256('boundedcode-second-validation-2026-10-05:' + instance_id); the four best-ranked are screened.",
    "Excluded: every instance used in development or the first validation (gin-3227, caddy-6288, prometheus-13845, vuejs-11899, axios-6539, grpc-go-2744, go-zero-2283, go-zero-990) and gold patches changing dependency manifests.",
    "Gate 1 (environment): acceptance fails on base and passes with the gold patch in the offline sandbox (Go 1.27, node 24).",
    "Gate 2 (derivability): a curator who sees the issue, base code, acceptance test and gold patch answers whether a competent engineer seeing only the issue could derive every behaviour the acceptance test requires (YES/NO/AMBIGUOUS), reproducing the issue on base and gold where practical. Rejected on: gold does not fix the issue's reproduction; tests require unrelated behaviour, exact formatting not required by the issue, names/API shapes only the gold introduces, or one of several outcomes the issue allows; offline-unreproducible environment.",
    "Per slot, the best-ranked candidate passing both gates is selected; a slot with none is left empty (no forcing).",
    "The agent never sees hidden tests, gold patches or screening analysis; the screening record stays benchmark-internal."
  ],
